## Data Models Implementation Plan

### Problem Analysis
- Need to implement core data models for the application
- Required models: Projects, Invoices, and Bills
- Need to establish relationships between models
- Must use Prisma with SQLite database

### Solution Design
1. Data Models:
   - Project Model:
     - Name
     - Relationships to Invoices and Bills
   - Invoice Model:
     - Total amount
     - Date
     - Notes
     - Relationship to Project
   - Bill Model:
     - Total amount
     - Date
     - Notes
     - Relationship to Project

2. Implementation Approach:
   - Use Prisma schema
   - Implement one-to-many relationships
   - Add proper indexes
   - Include timestamps for all models

### Implementation Steps
- [x] Project Model
  - [x] Define basic schema
  - [x] Add relationships
  - [x] Add indexes
  - Success criteria: Project model created with proper fields

- [x] Invoice Model
  - [x] Define basic schema
  - [x] Add relationship to Project
  - [x] Add indexes
  - Success criteria: Invoice model with Project relationship

- [x] Bill Model
  - [x] Define basic schema
  - [x] Add relationship to Project
  - [x] Add indexes
  - Success criteria: Bill model with Project relationship

- [x] Database Migration
  - [x] Generate migration
  - [x] Apply migration
  - [x] Verify relationships
  - Success criteria: All models properly migrated

### Affected Components
- `/prisma/schema.prisma` - Database schema
- `/src/types` - TypeScript types
- `/src/lib` - Prisma client configuration

### Dependencies
- Existing User model
- Prisma ORM
- SQLite database

